  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nHello.\nI'm the person who submitted the <graph> tag, so you might know me from there.\n\nIn many password fields, you have an option to toggle the visibility of your password in the field. I tried to add it to my website. I noticed that there is no HTML-native way to toggle visibility of a password. You need JS, and SVG (if you want an eye).\n\nI thought up an HTML-native way to do this.\n\n`<input type=\"password\" visibility>`\n\nIt creates an eye on the far right of the input field, and clicking it makes the eye full (default is eye hidden).\n\nYou can also do this:\n\n`<input type=\"password\" character=\"*\" visibility>\n\nNow, when it is supposed to be ·, it becomes *. It can me multiple chars, and filling the quotes with nothing makes it empty.",
